      "title": "Jacinta Allan declares she’ll stand against any leadership challenger after Labor factions move against her",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/27/jacinta-allan-leadership-challenge-labor-faction-meeting-victoria-politics",
      "description": "<p>Victorian premier says she intends to contest any ballot as sources say delegation of ministers have urged her to stand down</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/jul/27/ausalert-emergency-warning-test-antisemitism-royal-commission-nsw-icac-inquiry-politics-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-victoria-jacinta-allan-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The Victorian premier, Jacinta Allan, has thrown down the gauntlet to Labor powerbrokers, vowing to fight any attempt to oust her as leader amid a push for her to stand down before parliament resumes this week.</p><p>Just four months before a state election, factional conveners from Labor’s left and right met on Sunday night to discuss whether Allan still had the support of a majority of the caucus. It is understood that the group agreed she did not.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/27/jacinta-allan-leadership-challenge-labor-faction-meeting-victoria-politics\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-07-27T00:42:05"
    },
    {
      "title": "AusAlert test: what time will national emergency warning siren sound on phones in Australia today? Here’s what to know",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/27/ausalert-national-alert-test-sound-emergency-warning-system-time-date",
      "description": "<p>National emergency test alert will be sent to all compatible mobile devices on 27 July, with domestic violence advocates advising how to turn off safe phones</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/jul/27/ausalert-emergency-warning-test-antisemitism-royal-commission-nsw-icac-inquiry-politics-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-victoria-jacinta-allan-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Virtually every phone in the country will blare an emergency siren at 2pm AEST on Monday 27 July as part of the first Australia-wide test of a new national warning system called AusAlert.</p><p>Most phones, and some smartwatches and tablets, will receive a pop-up notification and an alert sound that cannot be silenced – even if your device is on “do not disturb” or silent mode.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/27/ausalert-national-alert-test-sound-emergency-warning-system-time-date\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-07-27T00:06:47"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Get rid of them’: One Nation senator claims party will ‘remigrate’ illegal visa holders in resurfaced interview",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/27/get-rid-of-them-one-nation-senator-claims-party-will-remigrate-visa-holders-in-resurfaced-interview-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive:</strong> Malcolm Roberts uses white supremacist concept to describe the party’s plans for deporting 200,000 people from Australia</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/jul/27/ausalert-emergency-warning-test-antisemitism-royal-commission-nsw-icac-inquiry-politics-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-victoria-jacinta-allan-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Senator Malcolm Roberts claims One Nation wants to deport at least 200,000 people and has repeatedly referred to the far-right concept of “remigration” in podcast interviews and speeches to niche platforms.</p><p>In two recent podcasts, Roberts said One Nation wanted to deport 100,000 temporary residents as well as 100,000 international students – a total much higher than the party’s published policy. The senator said after those people were removed, he wanted to “start working on the higher numbers of people we need to get rid of”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/jul/27/get-rid-of-them-one-nation-senator-claims-party-will-remigrate-visa-holders-in-resurfaced-interview-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-07-26T15:00:17"
    },
    {
      "title": "Former NSW Liberal powerbroker at heart of Icac allegations now living in UK and not expected to appear",
